    m_Localized: Actions
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6919559553024
    m_Localized: 'Lose condition: an enemy brings the Sword back to its original
      altar.


      Each time a wave of enemies is defeated, a new wave spawns,
      with one additional enemy each time.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7426810290176
    m_Localized: 'Controls:


      Left Click: Select and perform action

      Right
      Click: Switch active action

      Mouse Wheel: Zoom in / Zoom out

      A
      | E: Rotate camera around the grid'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7591650631680
    m_Localized: "Each pawn has 2 actions per turn:\n\nMoving up to 2 tiles.\n\nIf
      the pawn does not have the crown, it may push an enemy.\n(If the enemy is pushed
      into a wall or another pawn, it is stunned for 1 turn and takes 1 damage. If
      it is pushed into a hole, it is instantly eliminated.)\n\nIf the pawn has the
      crown, it can throw it in a straight line or a diagonal line.\nIf the crown
      hits and kills an enemy, it returns to the player\u2019s hands.\nIf the enemy
      survives, the crown falls in front of them.\nThe crown gains damage each time
      it is passed between allied pawns. Its damage resets if it falls, deals damage,
      or is picked up by an enemy.\n\nIf a pawn is in a hole, it can only move 1
      tile to climb out."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7803655921664
    m_Localized: 'Enemies move up to 3 tiles toward the nearest player.

      If
      they become adjacent to the closest player and still have movement left, they
      push the player, pick up the crown, and then move 3 tiles toward the nearest
      altar.

      Once again, if they still have movement remaining, they place
      the crown on the altar.


      If enemies have no possible path toward the
      crown, they will instead move toward the nearest player without the crown.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
